<!-- ===== THE RILL =====
     Channel bed (kerbs / shadowed inner walls / silt) at a 0.44 m cross-section
     period, with the water strip on top.
     THE WATER IS BAY-ALIGNED.  terrain_water's u period is 1.16 m == the colonnade's
     real bay spacing == and the painted column reflection sits at u = 0.5, so each
     water geom spans exactly one bay CENTRED ON A COLUMN (x = 0.90 + i*1.16) and the
     inverted colonnade lands under the real colonnade.  That is the bible's one-frame
     test beat, baked: `reflectance` cannot deliver it on a decal lying on an infinite
     plane, because the reflected half-space is filled by the floor itself.
     The channel runs fountain -> gate and dives under the spawn apron rather than
     crossing it, because nothing may stand inside r = 0.9 m. -->
